            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0454" n="342" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg342"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24074/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Vice and Deputy Consul General Baugh to the Secretary
                        of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Baugh reports serious disturbances Hunan missions and the destruction of
                    Chang-sha customhouse and business houses, Says missionaries have been summoned
                    from the interior, that foreign war vessels have been dispatched to Chang-sha,
                    and that the legation has been fully informed.</p>
            </div>
